  "context_pill": "Section 33AB & NABARD Withdrawals",
  "example_summary": "M/s. Gomati P Ltd. calculates its taxable business income by adjusting book profits for Section 33AB deductions, adding back deemed income from misutilized NABARD withdrawals and premature asset sales, and applying Section 79 loss restrictions.",
  "source_provision": "### Statutory Summary Matrix: Section 33AB & NABARD Withdrawals\n\n| Statutory Provision | Core Condition / Threshold | Tax Treatment / Legal Consequence |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Section 33AB Deduction** | Lower of deposit made within specified time or 40% of business profits | Allowed as business deduction in the year of deposit |\n| **NABARD Withdrawal Utilization** | Must be used for approved scheme (e.g. machinery, godown, replanting) | Exempt from deemed income if utilized as per specified scheme |\n| **Non-Permissible Withdrawal u/s 33AB(7)** | Amount withdrawn but not utilized within PY or spent on ineligible items | Deemed as Profits and Gains of Business or Profession in that PY |\n| **Premature Asset Sale u/s 33AB(8)** | Sale of asset acquired out of deposit before expiry of 8 years | Cost of such asset is deemed as PGBP income in the year of sale |\n\n\n> [!IMPORTANT] Dual Deduction Restriction: No depreciation or business deduction is allowable on assets acquired out of special account withdrawals if the original deposit was already allowed as a deduction u/s 33AB.\n\n\n> [!WARNING] Deemed Income Trap: Unutilized withdrawal amounts at the end of the previous year automatically trigger deemed business income under Section 33AB.",
